{% comment %}
  {% doc %}
    Single entry point for ALL Shopflo markup: SVG defs/styles/scripts, the checkout and buy-now
    buttons, the shop-pass account login proxy, and the shared dummy popup the checkout/buy-now
    buttons animate into. This file is never rendered as itself - only ever via
    `{% render 'shopflo', type: '...' %}`. Everything below is written so an AI theme-editing
    agent (e.g. Shopify Sidekick) can read this doc alone and correctly add/wire up any piece of
    Shopflo without having to open assets/shopflo-script.js or guess at markup contracts.

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    HOW TO ADD SHOPFLO TO A THEME - do these in order:
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    1. RENDER THE SHARED ASSETS EXACTLY ONCE PER PAGE.
       `{% render 'shopflo', type: 'assets' %}` outputs the SVG defs, the settings-driven <style>
       block (snippets/shopflo-css-variables.liquid), the Shopflo bundle's own <script> tags, this
       theme's assets/shopflo-script.js, and the shared dummy-popup overlay markup
       (#popupOverlay/#popupWrapper) that checkout/buy-now buttons animate into. It belongs in
       layout/theme.liquid (once, near the end of <body>). Every other `type` depends on this
       having rendered SOMEWHERE on the page - never render it more than once, and never render
       any other `type` on a page/layout that doesn't also render this one.

    2. RENDER THE CHECKOUT AND BUY-NOW BUTTONS WHERE THE THEME'S NATIVE ONES WOULD GO.
       `type: 'checkout'` replaces the theme's native "Check out" button (cart page, cart drawer,
       cart notification popup). `type: 'buy_now'` replaces a dynamic checkout/buy-now button
       (product page, product block). Just render it directly, unconditionally - there is NO
       Liquid-level enable/disable check anywhere, not at the call site and not in this file.
       Master on/off is the hardcoded `shopflo_enable` value in window.shopfloThemeConfig (see the
       "Master on/off" comment above the `{% case %}` below); assets/shopflo-script.js reads it at
       click time and decides there whether to open Shopflo's real checkout/cart or fall back to a
       plain navigation. Do not add a `settings.*` check, a `{% capture %}`/blank-check, or any
       other conditional around these render calls - see sections/main-cart-footer.liquid,
       snippets/cart-drawer.liquid, snippets/cart-notification.liquid, or snippets/buy-buttons.liquid
       for the plain unconditional call.

    3. RENDER THE ACCOUNT/LOGIN ICON WHERE THE THEME'S NATIVE ACCOUNT LINK WOULD GO.
       There are three independently-styled slots - `type: 'shop_pass_primary'`,
       `type: 'shop_pass_secondary'`, and `type: 'shop_pass_tertiary'` (the third exists for cases
       where two placements aren't enough, e.g. a footer or sidebar account link in addition to
       header/mobile-menu) - render any/all of them together, wherever an account control should
       appear, NOT picking a "desktop" vs "mobile" render location. Each instance decides for
       ITSELF whether it's actually visible at the current viewport width via its own "Device
       visibility" setting (Theme Editor > Shopflo Shop Pass > Login Button A/B/C > Device
       visibility: Desktop only / Mobile only / Both) - this is enforced purely with a CSS media
       query (see .sf-account-visible--desktop-only / --mobile-only in assets/shopflo-styles.css),
       so wherever you render them, they show/hide themselves correctly at every breakpoint with
       no extra Liquid logic needed. They stay in sync with each other automatically regardless
       (see <shopflo-accounts> in assets/shopflo-script.js). Button B and Button C each have their
       own "Inherit styles from" dropdown - Button B can inherit Button A or Button C; Button C can
       inherit Button A or Button B (Button A is the root, it has no such setting). EVERY instance
       you render must be wrapped in
       `settings.shopflo_customer_account_enabled == 'shopflo'` (Theme Editor > Shopflo Shop Pass >
       User Login), falling back to Shopify's native account link (`routes.account_url` /
       `routes.account_login_url` + `{% render 'icon-account' %}`) otherwise - copy the pattern in
       sections/header.liquid.

       NOTE: if you render an instance inside Dawn's <menu-drawer>/<header-drawer> (e.g. the
       mobile hamburger menu's utility-links row), its icon-toggle and "Log out" buttons already
       carry Dawn's own `localization-selector` class - the one thing that opts a button OUT of
       MenuDrawer.bindEvents()'s `button:not(.localization-selector)` "any button click closes the
       whole nav drawer" behavior in assets/global.js. Without it, merely toggling the account
       dropdown open/closed would also close the surrounding mobile nav. The "Account" drawer item
       deliberately does NOT carry it, since navigating to the account view SHOULD close the mobile
       nav drawer around it.

    4. IF YOU RENDER ANY shop_pass_primary/shop_pass_secondary/shop_pass_tertiary, ALSO RENDER
       `{% render 'shopflo', type: 'shop_pass_bundle_markup' %}` ONCE, ANYWHERE IN <body>.
       This is dummy, permanently-hidden markup that exists PURELY to satisfy the Shopflo bundle
       script's OWN internal getElementById/onclick lookups - the bundle silently fails its own
       initialization (never defining window.handleDrawer / window.handleShopifyLogin) without it,
       which breaks every shop_pass_primary/secondary/tertiary instance too, since they call those
       same globals. shop_pass_primary/secondary/tertiary themselves do NOT read from or forward
       clicks to this markup - only the bundle does. Skip this step entirely if you're not
       rendering any shop_pass_* instance on this theme.

    5. KEEP THE CART COUNT BADGE IN SYNC - see "CART COUNT SYNC" below.

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    CART TRIGGERS - how any element (not just this snippet's own buttons) can trigger Shopflo:
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    - ADD-TO-CART dispatches the custom DOM event `shopflo-event:add-to-cart` on `document` right
      after a successful add-to-cart (see assets/cart-drawer.js / assets/cart-notification.js).
      `bindDomEvents()` in assets/shopflo-script.js listens for it and opens Shopflo's cart
      immediately - the only cart-opening flow this theme wires up, so dispatch it unconditionally
      on every add-to-cart from shared/base theme code - falling back to a plain `/cart`
      navigation (same fallback as the cart icon's `openThemeFloCart()`) whenever
      shouldTriggerFloDirectly() is false (shopflo_enable off, or an internationally-redirected
      shopper).

    - To open Shopflo's CHECKOUT the same way: use the global `window.openThemeFloCheckout()`
      directly (`onclick="openThemeFloCheckout()"`) for any custom checkout/buy-link that isn't
      one of this snippet's own buttons - there is no data-attribute/event convention for checkout.

    - The header cart ICON (e.g. sections/header.liquid's `<a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}">`) is a
      plain link to the cart PAGE with no Shopflo wiring by default - clicking it just navigates
      there normally. Set `shopflo_intercept_cart_page_redirect: true` in the `window.shopfloThemeConfig`
      literal below (off by default, same hardcoded-not-a-setting convention as `shopflo_enable`)
      to have `bindCartPageRedirectIntercept()` in assets/shopflo-script.js intercept clicks on
      ANY link whose href resolves to `routes.cart_url` and open Shopflo's cart instead - no markup
      changes needed at the link itself.

    - ANIMATED checkout/buy-now buttons (the button -> full-screen popup FLIP animation): give the
      button `class="shopflo-popup-trigger"` plus `data-flo-action="checkout"` or
      `data-flo-action="buy-now"` - no `onclick` needed, assets/shopflo-script.js binds one
      delegated document-level click listener for every `.shopflo-popup-trigger` on the page (see
      `bindPopupMorph()`). This is exactly what `type: 'checkout'` (`#flo-checkout-button`) and
      `type: 'buy_now'` (`#flo-buy-now-button`) already render internally - only relevant if
      adding an EXTRA custom button elsewhere that should share the same animated flow instead of
      calling `openThemeFloCheckout()`/`handleFloBuyNowBtn()` directly (which still works, just
      without the popup animation).

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    CART COUNT SYNC - keeping a cart count badge live while Shopflo's cart/checkout is open:
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Add the class `flo-cart-icon-bubble` to whichever element renders the cart count badge
    anywhere in the theme (i.e. wherever `cart.item_count` / `cart.count` is output as a number
    next to a cart icon - typically a small pill/bubble, e.g. sections/header.liquid's
    `.cart-count-bubble`). Add it ALONGSIDE any existing class already used for the theme's own
    native styling/update behavior - do not replace it:

      <div class="cart-count-bubble flo-cart-icon-bubble">
        <span aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
      </div>

    Once tagged, Shopflo's own cart/checkout bundle (loaded by `type: 'assets'`) keeps that
    element's count in sync live whenever the customer adds, removes, or changes item quantities
    inside Shopflo's OWN cart drawer or checkout overlay - so the header badge never goes stale
    even though the customer never left the page or triggered a normal Shopify
    cart/add.js-driven re-render. This sync is handled entirely by the Shopflo bundle itself;
    no extra code is needed in this theme beyond adding the class to the right element.

    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    OUTBOUND EVENTS - so OTHER code (other apps' modals/popups, custom theme code) can react
    whenever Shopflo is about to visually open something, e.g. to close themselves out of the way:
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    - `shopflo-event:checkout-opened` - dispatched on `document` right before Shopflo's real
      checkout overlay opens, whether triggered by the checkout button or a buy-now button (both
      open the same underlying checkout, so there's only one event for either) - see
      `dispatchCheckoutOpened()` in assets/shopflo-script.js. NOT dispatched when Shopflo falls
      back to a plain `/checkout` navigation instead (nothing in-page is left to close then).

    - `shopflo-event:cart-opened` - dispatched on `document` right before Shopflo's real cart
      overlay opens, whether from a cart-icon click or an "Auto Open" auto-open after add-to-cart
      - see `dispatchCartOpened()` in assets/shopflo-script.js. NOT dispatched for the silent
      background cart load that happens on add-to-cart under "Cart Click" behavior (nothing
      becomes visible then), and NOT dispatched on the plain `/cart` navigation fallback.

    Shop-pass (account/login) interactions - dispatched by the <shopflo-accounts> custom element
    itself (see `_dispatchAccountEvent()` in assets/shopflo-script.js), from whichever
    shop_pass_primary/shop_pass_secondary/shop_pass_tertiary instance the shopper actually
    interacted with. Real auth state is read straight from two sessionStorage keys the Shopflo
    bundle itself keeps up to date - `flo_isShopfloSession` and `FLO_SSO_IS_LOGOUT` - there is no
    hidden markup, DOM observation, or click-forwarding involved for auth detection itself:

    - `shopflo-event:account-drawer-opened` / `shopflo-event:account-drawer-closed` - this theme's
      OWN Account/Log out dropdown menu, shown only when confidently logged in (a Shopflo session
      exists and no logout is in progress).

    - `shopflo-event:account-login-opened` - dispatched right before handing a header-icon click to
      Shopflo's own `window.handleDrawer()` - covers every state that isn't confidently logged in
      (fresh session, or just logged out), since the bundle itself decides whether to show its
      login UI or its own account drawer there. Bundle-rendered, not anything this theme renders
      itself, so there's no matching "closed" event - we have no signal for when it closes.

    - `shopflo-event:account-iframe-opened` / `shopflo-event:account-iframe-closed` - the account
      management SSO iframe view opened from the drawer's own "Account" item. Fired on BOTH desktop
      and mobile for "opened" (on mobile it's the bundle's own real sheet doing the opening, not
      our own proxy markup, but it's still a real shop-pass interaction worth notifying about) -
      but "closed" only fires on desktop, for the same no-signal-from-the-bundle reason as
      account-login-opened above. DESKTOP ONLY (800px+): the bundle's real login iframe (appended
      on `handleShopifyLogin()`) is kept permanently off-screen (see `#flo-shopify-login-iframe` in
      assets/shopflo-styles.css) - only its src is copied into this theme's own iframe, which is
      what's actually shown. MOBILE (up to 799px): the bundle's own real sheet+overlay+iframe is
      left fully visible and untouched instead.

    Listen for any of these the same way you'd listen for any DOM event:

      document.addEventListener('shopflo-event:checkout-opened', () => myModal.close());
      document.addEventListener('shopflo-event:cart-opened', () => myOtherPopup.close());
      document.addEventListener('shopflo-event:account-drawer-opened', () => myModal.close());

    @param {string} type - Which piece to render: 'assets' (svg defs/styles/scripts + shared popup markup, default), 'checkout' (checkout button), 'buy_now' (buy-now button), 'shop_pass_primary', 'shop_pass_secondary', or 'shop_pass_tertiary' (account login icon/drawer proxy, independently styled per slot, each self-hiding per its own "Visible on" setting - see <shopflo-accounts> in assets/shopflo-script.js), or 'shop_pass_bundle_markup' (dummy hidden markup the Shopflo bundle script itself needs to initialize correctly - required, once anywhere in <body>, whenever you render any shop_pass_* instance).
    @param {boolean} [shopflo_badge] - Checkout/buy_now only. Shows the "Powered by Shopflo" badge on the button. Defaults to true.
    @param {boolean} [shopflo_payment_icons] - Checkout/buy_now only. Master show/hide for the payment icons row, on top of (not instead of) the existing Theme Editor settings - Theme Editor > Shopflo Checkout/Buy Now > Show payment icons, icon 1/2/3 pickers, position, etc. all still apply exactly as before; this just lets a caller force the row off for one particular render (e.g. a compact cart-drawer instance) without touching those settings. Defaults to true. Pass `false` explicitly to hide - like `show_icon` below, NOT read via the `| default:` filter, since that would silently treat an explicit `false` the same as "not passed".
    @param {object} [form] - Required when type is 'buy_now'. The product form object, used for the dynamic Shopify payment button fallback.
    @param {object} [product_obj] - Required when type is 'buy_now'. The product object, used for checking stock.
    @param {string} [label_account] - shop_pass_primary/shop_pass_secondary/shop_pass_tertiary only. Drawer's account menu item label. Defaults to "Account".
    @param {string} [label_logout] - shop_pass_primary/shop_pass_secondary/shop_pass_tertiary only. Drawer's logout menu item label. Defaults to "Log out".
    @param {boolean} [show_icon] - shop_pass_primary/shop_pass_secondary/shop_pass_tertiary only. Whether to render the <svg> icon in either button state. Defaults to true. Pass `false` explicitly for a text-only instance - unlike other boolean params here, this one is NOT read via the `| default:` filter, since that would silently treat an explicit `false` the same as "not passed".

    @example
    Render the shared assets once in the theme layout, near the end of <body>:
  {% render 'shopflo', type: 'assets' %}
    @example
    Render the checkout button, optionally hiding the badge. No enable/disable check needed at the
    call site - just render it directly, unconditionally:
  {% render 'shopflo', type: 'checkout', shopflo_badge: true %}
    @example
    Render the buy-now button (requires the product form and product object; same unconditional call, no enable/disable check):
  {% render 'shopflo', type: 'buy_now', product_obj: product, form: form, shopflo_badge: true %}
    @example
    Render the account login icon/drawer slots together, in the SAME place (e.g. the header's
    account-icon spot) - each is styled independently via Theme Editor > Shopflo Shop Pass >
    Login Button A/B/C (Button B/C mirror another button's style settings when their own "Inherit
    styles from" points at one), and each shows/hides itself via its own "Device visibility"
    setting (Desktop only / Mobile only / Both) - no separate desktop/mobile render locations
    needed. Tertiary (Button C) is optional - only render it if you actually need a third
    independently-placed/styled instance (e.g. a footer or sidebar account link in addition to
    header/mobile-menu); most themes only need Primary + Secondary (Button A + Button B). Guard
    every instance you render with settings.shopflo_customer_account_enabled == 'shopflo',
    falling back to a native account link:
  {% render 'shopflo', type: 'shop_pass_primary' %}
  {% render 'shopflo', type: 'shop_pass_secondary' %}
  {% render 'shopflo', type: 'shop_pass_tertiary' %}
    @example
    Required exactly once, anywhere in <body>, on any page/layout that renders shop_pass_primary/
    shop_pass_secondary/shop_pass_tertiary - typically alongside `type: 'assets'` in
    layout/theme.liquid. Skip it entirely if this theme never renders a shop_pass_* instance:
  {% render 'shopflo', type: 'shop_pass_bundle_markup' %}
    @example
    Tag a cart icon's count badge for live sync:
  <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" id="cart-icon-bubble" class="header__icon header__icon--cart">
    {% render 'icon-cart' %}
    <div class="cart-count-bubble flo-cart-icon-bubble">
      <span aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.item_count }}</span>
    </div>
  </a>
  {% enddoc %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign shopflo_snippet_type = type | default: 'assets'
  assign shopflo_badge = shopflo_badge | default: true

  # NOT `shopflo_payment_icons | default: true` - see the @param doc above: the default filter
  # would silently treat an explicit `false` the same as "not passed".
  assign shopflo_payment_icons_param = shopflo_payment_icons
  assign shopflo_payment_icons = true
  if shopflo_payment_icons_param == false
    assign shopflo_payment_icons = false
  endif

  assign any_selected_checkout_payment_icons = false
  if settings.shopflo_payment_icon_1_checkout != 'none' or settings.shopflo_payment_icon_2_checkout != 'none' or settings.shopflo_payment_icon_3_checkout != 'none'
    assign any_selected_checkout_payment_icons = true
  endif

  assign any_selected_buy_now_payment_icons = false
  if settings.shopflo_payment_icon_1_buy_now != 'none' or settings.shopflo_payment_icon_2_buy_now != 'none' or settings.shopflo_payment_icon_3_buy_now != 'none'
    assign any_selected_buy_now_payment_icons = true
  endif
-%}

{% comment %}
  Master on/off: NOT a Theme Editor setting and NOT a Liquid condition anywhere in this file or
  its callers - 'checkout'/'buy_now' below always render the same Shopflo markup unconditionally.
  The single source of truth is the hardcoded `shopflo_enable` value in window.shopfloThemeConfig
  (below, in the 'assets' branch). assets/shopflo-script.js reads this.config.shopflo_enable at
  click time (see `shouldTriggerFloDirectly()`) and decides THERE whether to open Shopflo's real
  checkout/cart or fall back to a plain navigation - the button markup itself never changes.
{% endcomment %}

{% case shopflo_snippet_type %}
  {% when 'assets' %}
    <script src="https://bridge.shopflo.com/js/shopflo.bundle.js" async></script>

    {%- liquid
      # Resolves EVERY style field for Button B/Button C (icon size/color, button background,
      # padding, radius, text color, and the 6 shadow fields) against Theme Editor > Shopflo
      # Shop Pass > Login Button B/C > "Inherit styles from" - Button B can inherit Button A or
      # Button C; Button C can inherit Button A or Button B (Button A is the root - it never
      # inherits from anything, so it has no such setting). Since B can point at C AND C can
      # point at B at the same time, a naive single-pass resolution could reference a value that
      # isn't computed yet - or, if a shopper sets BOTH to inherit from each other, chase its own
      # tail forever. Liquid can't recurse or loop this dynamically (no functions, no dynamic
      # property lookup), so this resolves in two fixed passes instead:
      #
      #   1. B_PRELIM: resolve B against A directly, or against C's OWN raw fields (not yet
      #      knowing whether C itself inherits from anything - a deliberately shallow read).
      #   2. C_FINAL: resolve C against A directly, or against B_PRELIM (so if B inherits from
      #      A, C inheriting from B correctly ends up with A's values too).
      #   3. B_FINAL: same as B_PRELIM, EXCEPT when B inherits from C, use C_FINAL instead of
      #      C's raw fields (so if C inherits from A, B inheriting from C correctly ends up with
      #      A's values too).
      #
      # In the genuine cycle case (B inherits C AND C inherits B), this still always terminates:
      # B_PRELIM reads C's raw fields, C_FINAL then resolves to that same raw value, and B_FINAL
      # resolves to C_FINAL - so both sides settle on Button C's own raw fields. Not what either
      # setting says in isolation, but a safe, deterministic fallback rather than an infinite
      # chase - exactly the kind of edge case a merchant could accidentally create by pointing
      # both dropdowns at each other.

      assign account_font_size_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_font_size_button_b
      assign account_icon_gap_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_icon_gap_button_b
      assign account_icon_size_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_icon_size_button_b
      assign account_icon_color_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_icon_color_button_b
      assign account_button_background_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_button_background_button_b
      assign account_padding_block_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_padding_block_button_b
      assign account_padding_inline_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_padding_inline_button_b
      assign account_button_radius_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_button_radius_button_b
      assign account_color_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_color_button_b
      assign account_shadow_enabled_button_b_preliminary = settings.show_shopflo_account_button_shadow_button_b
      assign account_shadow_inset_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_inset_button_b
      assign account_shadow_horizontal_offset_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_horizontal_offset_button_b
      assign account_shadow_vertical_offset_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_vertical_offset_button_b
      assign account_shadow_blur_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_blur_button_b
      assign account_shadow_spread_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_spread_button_b
      assign account_shadow_color_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_color_button_b
      if settings.shopflo_account_match_with_button_b == 'button_a'
        assign account_font_size_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_font_size_button_a
        assign account_icon_gap_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_icon_gap_button_a
        assign account_icon_size_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_icon_size_button_a
        assign account_icon_color_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_icon_color_button_a
        assign account_button_background_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_button_background_button_a
        assign account_padding_block_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_padding_block_button_a
        assign account_padding_inline_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_padding_inline_button_a
        assign account_button_radius_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_button_radius_button_a
        assign account_color_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_color_button_a
        assign account_shadow_enabled_button_b_preliminary = settings.show_shopflo_account_button_shadow_button_a
        assign account_shadow_inset_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_inset_button_a
        assign account_shadow_horizontal_offset_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_horizontal_offset_button_a
        assign account_shadow_vertical_offset_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_vertical_offset_button_a
        assign account_shadow_blur_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_blur_button_a
        assign account_shadow_spread_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_spread_button_a
        assign account_shadow_color_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_color_button_a
      elsif settings.shopflo_account_match_with_button_b == 'button_c'
        assign account_font_size_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_font_size_button_c
        assign account_icon_gap_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_icon_gap_button_c
        assign account_icon_size_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_icon_size_button_c
        assign account_icon_color_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_icon_color_button_c
        assign account_button_background_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_button_background_button_c
        assign account_padding_block_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_padding_block_button_c
        assign account_padding_inline_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_padding_inline_button_c
        assign account_button_radius_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_button_radius_button_c
        assign account_color_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_color_button_c
        assign account_shadow_enabled_button_b_preliminary = settings.show_shopflo_account_button_shadow_button_c
        assign account_shadow_inset_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_inset_button_c
        assign account_shadow_horizontal_offset_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_horizontal_offset_button_c
        assign account_shadow_vertical_offset_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_vertical_offset_button_c
        assign account_shadow_blur_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_blur_button_c
        assign account_shadow_spread_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_spread_button_c
        assign account_shadow_color_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_color_button_c
      endif

      assign account_font_size_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_font_size_button_c
      assign account_icon_gap_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_icon_gap_button_c
      assign account_icon_size_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_icon_size_button_c
      assign account_icon_color_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_icon_color_button_c
      assign account_button_background_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_button_background_button_c
      assign account_padding_block_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_padding_block_button_c
      assign account_padding_inline_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_padding_inline_button_c
      assign account_button_radius_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_button_radius_button_c
      assign account_color_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_color_button_c
      assign account_shadow_enabled_button_c_source = settings.show_shopflo_account_button_shadow_button_c
      assign account_shadow_inset_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_inset_button_c
      assign account_shadow_horizontal_offset_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_horizontal_offset_button_c
      assign account_shadow_vertical_offset_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_vertical_offset_button_c
      assign account_shadow_blur_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_blur_button_c
      assign account_shadow_spread_button_c_source = settings.shopflo_account_shadow_spread_button_c
