  {% when 'shop_pass_bundle_markup' %}
    {%- comment -%}
      Dummy markup that exists PURELY to satisfy the Shopflo bundle script's OWN internal
      getElementById/onclick lookups - it expects these exact ids to exist somewhere in the DOM
      for its own account/login wiring to initialize correctly, independently of anything this
      theme itself reads or writes. shop_pass_primary/shop_pass_secondary/shop_pass_tertiary
      (see <shopflo-accounts> in assets/shopflo-script.js) do NOT read from or forward clicks to
      any of this - they're driven entirely by their own sessionStorage-based logic. This exists
      only because the bundle itself silently fails its own initialization (never defining
      window.handleDrawer / window.handleShopifyLogin) when it can't find this markup, which
      breaks shop_pass_primary/secondary/tertiary too, since they call those same globals.

      Covers BOTH variants the bundle's header script builds: the desktop set
      (#flo-login-button-header-logo / #loggedin-icons / #icon-close-shopflo / #icon-shopflo /
      #shopflo-drawer-desktop / #account-button-desktop / #logout-button-desktop) and the
      "-mobile" suffixed equivalents (#flo-login-button-header-logo-mobile /
      #loggedin-icons-mobile / #icon-close-shopflo-mobile / #icon-shopflo-mobile /
      #shopflo-drawer-mobile / #logout-button-mobile). The mobile drawer's account link has no
      id in the bundle's own markup either - only the desktop one gets #account-button-desktop -
      so none is added here. Both sets are required: the bundle's init runs the same
      getElementById lookups regardless of viewport, so omitting the mobile half reproduces the
      exact same silent-failure bug this markup exists to prevent, just on small screens.

      Render this ONCE, ANYWHERE in <body> (not <head> - a <div>/<button> isn't valid there, and
      while browsers do silently relocate invalid head content to the start of body per the HTML
      parsing spec, that's not something to rely on for markup you're intentionally adding).
      Order relative to shop_pass_primary/secondary/tertiary or the bundle's own <script> tag
      doesn't matter - the onclick attributes below resolve window.handleDrawer/
      handleShopifyLogin lazily at click time, not at parse time.

      Kept permanently off-screen via .shopflo-accounts-hidden (position: fixed; left:
      -99999px; ...) in assets/shopflo-styles.css - NOT display:none/visibility:hidden/zero-size
      clipping. The bundle's own scripts toggle inline styles on these elements directly, and
      either hiding technique can silently fight that, and zero-size clipping breaks
      handleDrawer's internal position:absolute layout for the (also-hidden, unused) drawers
      below. .header--icon and .header--icon--mobile both stay on the wrapper too, since the
      bundle's header script also uses them as its own "already injected, skip" guards
      (querySelector(".header--icon") / querySelector(".header--icon--mobile")) before building
      the real desktop/mobile replacement nodes - dropping either class here would just move the
      missing-markup failure from "globals never defined" to "guard never satisfied," not fix it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div
      id="shopflo-accounts-hidden-root"
      class="shopflo-accounts-hidden header--icon header--icon--mobile"
      aria-hidden="true"
      inert
    >
      {%- comment -%} Desktop {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- comment -%} Not-logged-in trigger — bundle wires this by id (getElementById), not inline onclick. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div id="flo-login-button-header-logo" tabindex="-1"></div>

      {%- comment -%} Logged-in icon + close icon — toggled by handleDrawer(). {%- endcomment -%}
      <div id="loggedin-icons">
        <div id="icon-close-shopflo" onclick="handleDrawer()" tabindex="-1"></div>
        <div id="icon-shopflo" onclick="handleDrawer()" tabindex="-1"></div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Dropdown drawer — display/position toggled by handleDrawer().
        Kept as a real, normally-laid-out box (not clipped to zero size)
        so handleDrawer's internal absolute positioning keeps working —
        only the outer wrapper above is moved off-screen (see CSS).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div id="shopflo-drawer-desktop">
        <ul>
          <a
            id="account-button-desktop"
            href="javascript:void(0);"
            onclick="handleShopifyLogin(event,'/account')"
            tabindex="-1"
          >
            <p>Account</p>
          </a>
        </ul>
        <button id="logout-button-desktop" type="button" tabindex="-1"><p>Log out</p></button>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Mobile — same ids/wiring as desktop above, "-mobile" suffixed. {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- comment -%} Not-logged-in trigger — bundle wires this by id (getElementById), not inline onclick. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div id="flo-login-button-header-logo-mobile" tabindex="-1"></div>

      {%- comment -%} Logged-in icon + close icon — toggled by handleDrawer(). {%- endcomment -%}
      <div id="loggedin-icons-mobile">
        <div id="icon-close-shopflo-mobile" onclick="handleDrawer()" tabindex="-1"></div>
        <div id="icon-shopflo-mobile" onclick="handleDrawer()" tabindex="-1"></div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Dropdown drawer — display/position toggled by handleDrawer().
        No id on this account link — the bundle's own mobile markup doesn't give it one
        either (only #account-button-desktop exists on the desktop side).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div id="shopflo-drawer-mobile">
        <ul>
          <a
            href="javascript:void(0);"
            onclick="handleShopifyLogin(event,'/account')"
            tabindex="-1"
          >
            <p>Account</p>
          </a>
        </ul>
        <button id="logout-button-mobile" type="button" tabindex="-1"><p>Logout</p></button>
      </div>
    </div>

  {% when 'checkout' %}
    {%- liquid
      assign checkout_icon_1 = settings.shopflo_payment_icon_checkout_1
      assign checkout_icon_2 = settings.shopflo_payment_icon_checkout_2
      assign checkout_icon_3 = settings.shopflo_payment_icon_checkout_3
      assign checkout_icons_list = checkout_icon_1 | append: '|' | append: checkout_icon_2 | append: '|' | append: checkout_icon_3 | split: '|'

      # shopflo_payment_icons (render param, see @doc above) is an extra AND-gate on top of the
      # Theme Editor's own "Show payment icons" setting - both still have to be true for the row
      # to render.
      assign checkout_icons_enabled = settings.shopflo_payment_icons_checkout
      if shopflo_payment_icons == false
        assign checkout_icons_enabled = false
      endif

      assign any_selected_checkout_payment_icons = false
      if checkout_icon_1 != 'none' or checkout_icon_2 != 'none' or checkout_icon_3 != 'none'
        assign any_selected_checkout_payment_icons = true
      endif

      # Badge SVG defs (filter/gradient) below must have unique ids per render - a cart drawer's
      # checkout button (hidden until opened) coexists in the DOM with e.g. a product page's
      # buy-now button on the very same page, and this same badge markup is duplicated in the
      # 'buy_now' case below too. section.id keys it to whichever section rendered this call.
      assign shopflo_badge_uid = section.id | append: '-checkout' | default: 'checkout'

      # richtext setting - a merchant-cleared field can still come back as e.g. "<p></p>" or
      # "<p>&nbsp;</p>" (non-blank as raw HTML), so strip tags/nbsp before checking presence.
      # Computed BEFORE checkout_wrapper_class below - that capture's sf-promo-banner__layout--*
      # class must agree with whether the promo div actually renders, or the button ends up
      # styled (e.g. flat-topped border-radius) for a banner that was never rendered at all.
      assign shopflo_promo_text_check = settings.shopflo_promo_text_checkout | strip_html | remove: '&nbsp;' | strip
      assign shopflo_promo_text_checkout_present = false
      unless shopflo_promo_text_check == blank
        assign shopflo_promo_text_checkout_present = true
      endunless
    -%}

    {% capture checkout_wrapper_class %} shopflo-checkout__wrapper {% if settings.shopflo_full_width_checkout == true %} sf-full-width {% endif %} {% if shopflo_promo_text_checkout_present %} sf-promo-banner__layout--{{ settings.shopflo_promo_banner_layout_checkout }} {% endif %}{% endcapture %}

    {% capture checkout_button_class %}
    shopflo-checkout__button shopflo-popup-trigger {% if settings.shopflo_full_width_checkout == true %} sf-full-width {% endif %} {% if settings.shopflo_shadow_style_checkout != 'none' %} sf-button-shadow--{{ settings.shopflo_shadow_style_checkout }} {%
    endif %} {% if settings.shopflo_hover_effect_checkout != 'none' %} sf-button-hover--{{ settings.shopflo_hover_effect_checkout }} {% endif %} {% if checkout_icons_enabled == true %} sf-checkout-payment-icon--{{ settings.shopflo_payment_icon_position_checkout }} {% endif %}
    {% endcapture %}

    {%- capture checkout_promo_markup -%}
      {%- if shopflo_promo_text_checkout_present -%}
        <div class="shopflo-checkout--promo sf-full-width sf-label--{{ settings.shopflo_promo_text_alignment_checkout }} sf-promo-position--{{ settings.shopflo_promo_position_checkout }}">
          <span class="shopflo-checkout--promo__text">{{ settings.shopflo_promo_text_checkout }}</span>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

