  {% when 'shop_pass_primary', 'shop_pass_secondary', 'shop_pass_tertiary' %}
    {%- comment -%}
      Account/login icon + dropdown proxy. Three independent, fully separately-styled slots -
      type: 'shop_pass_primary', type: 'shop_pass_secondary', and type: 'shop_pass_tertiary'
      (Theme Editor > Shopflo Shop Pass > Login Button A/B/C) - each with its own icon
      size/color/padding/radius/label settings, AND its own "Device visibility" setting
      (Desktop only / Mobile only / Both), enforced purely via CSS media query (see
      .sf-account-visible--desktop-only / --mobile-only in assets/shopflo-styles.css). Render
      any/all of them together, wherever an account control should appear - there's no need to
      pick a "desktop" vs "mobile" render location, each instance hides/shows itself at the
      right breakpoint on its own. Safe to render multiple times on the same page regardless:
      every instance is fully independent and reads the SAME two sessionStorage keys directly for
      auth state - there is no cross-instance sync to maintain, since logging out reloads the
      page (every instance just re-reads the keys fresh on load). The one thing still shared
      across instances is the bundle's real login iframe. DESKTOP ONLY (800px+): it's kept
      permanently off-screen (see #flo-shopify-login-iframe in assets/shopflo-styles.css), and
      each instance's "Account" click copies its src into that instance's OWN iframe, so the
      visible copy is always local to whichever slot the shopper clicked. MOBILE (up to 799px):
      left fully untouched - the bundle's own real sheet+overlay+iframe renders and shows/hides
      itself, and this theme's own drawer/overlay just steps out of the way. See the
      <shopflo-accounts> custom element in assets/shopflo-script.js.

      Fully safe to restyle or restructure everything inside <shopflo-accounts>...</shopflo-accounts>
      - only the data-flo-trigger / data-flo-state attributes are load-bearing.

      NOTE: real logged-in/out state is resolved client-side from two sessionStorage keys the
      Shopflo bundle itself owns and keeps up to date - `flo_isShopfloSession` and
      `FLO_SSO_IS_LOGOUT` (both are either the string "true" or absent, never a literal "false") -
      not from Shopify's `customer` object, since Shopflo's own auth session is separate from
      Shopify's native customer session. Confidently "logged in" means a session exists AND no
      logout is in progress; every other combination defers the click straight to the bundle's
      own `window.handleDrawer()` rather than guessing (see _resolveSessionState() in
      assets/shopflo-script.js). This is resolved fresh on every header-icon click, so it always
      reflects the current state, not whatever was true on page load.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign account_slot = 'primary'
      if shopflo_snippet_type == 'shop_pass_secondary'
        assign account_slot = 'secondary'
      elsif shopflo_snippet_type == 'shop_pass_tertiary'
        assign account_slot = 'tertiary'
      endif

      assign account_variant_class = 'shopflo-accounts--primary'
      assign account_iframe_id = 'shopflo-theme-accounts-iframe-primary'
      assign account_visible_on = settings.shopflo_account_visible_on_button_a
      assign account_drawer_position = settings.shopflo_account_dropdown_vertical_button_a
      if account_slot == 'secondary'
        assign account_variant_class = 'shopflo-accounts--secondary'
        assign account_iframe_id = 'shopflo-theme-accounts-iframe-secondary'
        assign account_visible_on = settings.shopflo_account_visible_on_button_b
        assign account_drawer_position = settings.shopflo_account_dropdown_vertical_button_b
      elsif account_slot == 'tertiary'
        assign account_variant_class = 'shopflo-accounts--tertiary'
        assign account_iframe_id = 'shopflo-theme-accounts-iframe-tertiary'
        assign account_visible_on = settings.shopflo_account_visible_on_button_c
        assign account_drawer_position = settings.shopflo_account_dropdown_vertical_button_c
      endif

      # "Dropdown position" (Theme Editor > Shopflo Shop Pass > Login Button A/B/C) is ONE
      # combined setting ("above-left" / "above-right" / "below-left" / "below-right") - split
      # it into the two separate data attributes assets/shopflo-script.js's
      # _computeDrawerPosition() actually reads (data-drawer-vertical / data-drawer-horizontal),
      # so that file never needs to know this is stored as one dash-joined value rather than two.
      assign account_drawer_position_parts = account_drawer_position | split: '-'
      assign account_drawer_vertical = account_drawer_position_parts[0] | default: 'below'
      assign account_drawer_horizontal = account_drawer_position_parts[1] | default: 'right'

      # "Device visibility" is independent of "Inherit styles from" - it's a placement choice,
      # not a style one, so it always reads this slot's OWN setting even when styles are matched.
      case account_visible_on
        when 'desktop'
          assign account_visible_class = 'sf-account-visible--desktop-only'
        when 'mobile'
          assign account_visible_class = 'sf-account-visible--mobile-only'
        else
          assign account_visible_class = ''
      endcase

      # "Inherit styles from" (Theme Editor > Shopflo Shop Pass > Login Button B/C) hides that
      # slot's own text/layout fields and reads them straight off the matched slot instead -
      # Button B can inherit Button A or Button C; Button C can inherit Button A or Button B.
      # Since either can point at the other, this resolves in the same two-pass order as the
      # style vars above (see the long comment in the 'assets' case): B_PRELIM against A or C's
      # raw fields, then B_FINAL swapped to C_FINAL if B points at C - so a genuine A<-B<-C or
      # A<-C<-B chain resolves correctly, and a B<->C cycle still terminates (both settle on
      # Button C's own raw fields) rather than looping.
      assign account_label_text_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_text_button_b
      assign account_button_layout_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_button_layout_button_b
      assign account_bold_text_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_bold_text_button_b
      if settings.shopflo_account_match_with_button_b == 'button_a'
        assign account_label_text_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_text_button_a
        assign account_button_layout_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_button_layout_button_a
        assign account_bold_text_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_bold_text_button_a
      elsif settings.shopflo_account_match_with_button_b == 'button_c'
        assign account_label_text_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_text_button_c
        assign account_button_layout_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_button_layout_button_c
        assign account_bold_text_button_b_preliminary = settings.shopflo_account_bold_text_button_c
      endif

      assign account_label_text_button_c = settings.shopflo_account_text_button_c
      assign account_button_layout_button_c = settings.shopflo_account_button_layout_button_c
      assign account_bold_text_button_c = settings.shopflo_account_bold_text_button_c
      if settings.shopflo_account_match_with_button_c == 'button_a'
        assign account_label_text_button_c = settings.shopflo_account_text_button_a
        assign account_button_layout_button_c = settings.shopflo_account_button_layout_button_a
        assign account_bold_text_button_c = settings.shopflo_account_bold_text_button_a
      elsif settings.shopflo_account_match_with_button_c == 'button_b'
        assign account_label_text_button_c = account_label_text_button_b_preliminary
        assign account_button_layout_button_c = account_button_layout_button_b_preliminary
        assign account_bold_text_button_c = account_bold_text_button_b_preliminary
      endif

      assign account_label_text_button_b = account_label_text_button_b_preliminary
      assign account_button_layout_button_b = account_button_layout_button_b_preliminary
      assign account_bold_text_button_b = account_bold_text_button_b_preliminary
      if settings.shopflo_account_match_with_button_b == 'button_c'
        assign account_label_text_button_b = account_label_text_button_c
        assign account_button_layout_button_b = account_button_layout_button_c
        assign account_bold_text_button_b = account_bold_text_button_c
      endif

      if account_slot == 'primary'
        assign account_label_text = settings.shopflo_account_text_button_a
        assign account_button_layout = settings.shopflo_account_button_layout_button_a
        assign account_bold_text = settings.shopflo_account_bold_text_button_a
      elsif account_slot == 'secondary'
        assign account_label_text = account_label_text_button_b
        assign account_button_layout = account_button_layout_button_b
        assign account_bold_text = account_bold_text_button_b
      else
        assign account_label_text = account_label_text_button_c
        assign account_button_layout = account_button_layout_button_c
        assign account_bold_text = account_bold_text_button_c
      endif

      assign account_font_weight = 'normal'
      if account_bold_text
        assign account_font_weight = 'bold'
      endif

      assign label_account = label_account | default: 'Account'
      assign label_logout = label_logout | default: 'Log out'

      assign show_account_label = false
      if account_label_text != blank
        assign show_account_label = true
      endif

      # show_icon: whether to render the <svg> at all in either button state - a render
      # parameter (not a Theme Editor setting), so a caller can drop just the icon for a
      # particular instance (e.g. a text-only "Account" link somewhere) without affecting
      # every other shop_pass_primary/shop_pass_secondary/shop_pass_tertiary instance on the
      # page. Defaults to true - every existing call site keeps rendering the icon unchanged.
      # NOT `show_icon | default: true` - the default filter treats an explicit `false` the same
      # as "not passed" and would silently flip it back to true, defeating the parameter entirely.
      assign show_icon_param = show_icon
      assign show_icon = true
      if show_icon_param == false
        assign show_icon = false
      endif

      # localization-selector is Dawn's OWN opt-out marker (see button:not(.localization-selector)
      # in assets/global.js's MenuDrawer.bindEvents()) for buttons that must NOT close the
      # mobile nav drawer they happen to render inside (e.g. shop_pass_secondary in the header's
      # menu-drawer__utility-links) - added here purely to borrow that exclusion, not for its
      # literal localization styling/behavior (verified it has no effect without the sibling
      # classes/markup those rules require). Toggling the account dropdown open/closed should
      # never close the whole nav drawer around it. The "Account" drawer item deliberately does
      # NOT get this class - it's the one action that SHOULD close the nav drawer, since it opens
      # a real account view.
      assign account_icon_button_class = 'shopflo-accounts__icon-button localization-selector'
      if show_account_label and account_button_layout == 'icon_right'
        assign account_icon_button_class = account_icon_button_class | append: ' sf-account-layout--icon-right'
      endif
    -%}

    <shopflo-accounts
      class="shopflo-accounts {{ account_variant_class }} {{ account_visible_class }}"
      data-drawer-vertical="{{ account_drawer_vertical }}"
      data-drawer-horizontal="{{ account_drawer_horizontal }}"
    >
      {%- comment -%} Logged-out state: same header-icon trigger as the logged-in button below — real state decides where the click goes {%- endcomment -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="{{ account_icon_button_class }}"
        data-flo-trigger="header-icon"
        data-flo-state="login-icon"
        data-flo-visible="true"
        aria-label="Your account"
      >
        {%- if show_icon -%}
          <svg
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 29 29"
            fill="none"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <g stroke="currentColor">
              <path d="M4.833 25.375V22.958C4.833 21.677 5.343 20.447 6.249 19.541C7.155 18.634 8.385 18.125 9.667 18.125H12.688" stroke-width="1.611" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              <path d="M14.5 13.292C17.169 13.292 19.333 11.128 19.333 8.458C19.333 5.789 17.169 3.625 14.5 3.625C11.831 3.625 9.667 5.789 9.667 8.458C9.667 11.128 11.831 13.292 14.5 13.292Z" stroke-width="1.611" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </g>
            <path d="M21.387 12.3L14.171 20.617L20.514 20.743L19.697 26.367L26.912 18.05L20.57 17.924L21.387 12.3Z" fill="#01CCA7" stroke="#01CCA7" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if show_account_label -%}
          <span class="shopflo-accounts__label sf-text--{{ account_font_weight }}">{{ account_label_text }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </button>

      {%- comment -%} Logged-in state: same header-icon trigger, opens the proxy drawer once resolved state says logged-in {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="shopflo-accounts__logged-in" data-flo-state="account-icon" data-flo-visible="false">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="{{ account_icon_button_class }}"
          data-flo-trigger="header-icon"
          aria-label="Account menu"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-haspopup="true"
        >
          {%- if show_icon -%}
            <svg
              width="20"
              height="20"
              viewBox="0 0 29 29"
              fill="none"
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <g stroke="currentColor">
                <path d="M4.833 25.375V22.958C4.833 21.677 5.343 20.447 6.249 19.541C7.155 18.634 8.385 18.125 9.667 18.125H12.688" stroke-width="1.611" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                <path d="M14.5 13.292C17.169 13.292 19.333 11.128 19.333 8.458C19.333 5.789 17.169 3.625 14.5 3.625C11.831 3.625 9.667 5.789 9.667 8.458C9.667 11.128 11.831 13.292 14.5 13.292Z" stroke-width="1.611" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </g>
              <path d="M21.387 12.3L14.171 20.617L20.514 20.743L19.697 26.367L26.912 18.05L20.57 17.924L21.387 12.3Z" fill="#01CCA7" stroke="#01CCA7" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if show_account_label -%}
            <span class="shopflo-accounts__label sf-text--{{ account_font_weight }}">{{ account_label_text }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </button>

        <div class="shopflo-accounts__drawer" data-flo-state="drawer" data-flo-visible="false" role="menu">
          <ul class="shopflo-accounts__drawer-list">
            <li role="none">
              <button
                type="button"
                class="shopflo-accounts__drawer-item"
                role="menuitem"
                data-flo-trigger="account-login"
              >
                {{ label_account }}
              </button>
            </li>
            <li role="none">
              {%- comment -%}
                localization-selector: same nav-drawer-close opt-out as the header-icon buttons
                above - logging out reloads the page itself, so it doesn't need the theme's
                mobile nav drawer to close it first.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="shopflo-accounts__drawer-item localization-selector"
                role="menuitem"
                data-flo-trigger="account-logout"
              >
                {{ label_logout }}
              </button>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Our OWN copy of the account-login iframe, not the bundle's original — sibling of
          .shopflo-accounts__drawer. JS copies the src from the bundle's real
          #flo-shopify-login-iframe once it appears, into this one, since the real one is kept
          permanently off-screen (see assets/shopflo-styles.css) on every device, and this one
          lives in normal visible proxy markup that can be styled/positioned freely. The id is
          unique per slot (not otherwise load-bearing - the JS scopes lookups to this instance
          via data-flo-state) purely to keep valid, non-duplicate-id markup when multiple slots
          are rendered on the same page.

          IMPORTANT: if the iframe's content talks back to the parent page via postMessage keyed
          to a specific iframe reference, this copy will NOT receive that — verify the login
          flow actually completes end-to-end through this copy, not just that it renders.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <iframe
          src="about:blank"
          id="{{ account_iframe_id }}"
          class="shopflo-accounts__drawer-iframe"
          data-flo-state="drawer-iframe"
          data-flo-visible="false"
          title="Account"
        ></iframe>

        {%- comment -%}
          Closes the dropdown or iframe view - only ever shown while one of them is open, so a
          click on it always means "close", not a toggle.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div
          class="shopflo-accounts__overlay"
          data-flo-trigger="close-drawer"
          data-flo-state="account-drawer-overlay"
          data-flo-visible="false"
          aria-hidden="true"
        ></div>
      </div>
    </shopflo-accounts>
{% endcase %}
